  "summary": {
    "en": "Turkey has intensified airstrikes to support President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud, increasing civilian casualties, while Uganda is withdrawing its troops and peacekeepers are moving into bases near the capital. The United States has left the strategic Baledogle airfield, but joint airstrikes by U.S. forces and an East African nation continue against al-Shabaab. Somali forces, urged by the army chief, are intensifying operations against al-Shabaab near Barawe, and a Somali police officer was killed by an aircraft propeller at Dhusamareb Airport. The conflict caused 2,284 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
